Project Overview
This project is a Customer Segmentation Dashboard designed to analyze customer demographics, education levels, occupations, premium amounts, and communication preferences. The dashboard provides a consolidated view of customer data to help identify patterns, understand customer groups, and support data-driven business decisions.

Key Features
Analysis of customer age distribution across marital status categories.

Comparison of customers based on education levels.

Segmentation of customers by occupation.

Analysis of premium amounts across different education and gender groups.

Analysis of customer communication preferences.

Interactive dashboard elements for filtering and exploring customer segments.

Visual representation of customer data through charts and summary reports.

Business Objectives
The main objective of this project is to transform customer data into meaningful insights that can help businesses:

Understand different customer segments.

Identify customer groups with higher premium contributions.

Analyze demographic characteristics of customers.

Compare customer behavior across education and occupation categories.

Understand preferred communication channels.

Improve customer targeting and marketing strategies.

Support data-driven customer relationship management.

Dashboard Analysis
Customer Age Analysis
The dashboard summarizes customer age across different marital status categories, allowing users to compare the overall age distribution of customer groups.

Education Analysis
Customer data is categorized by education level, including Associate's Degree, Bachelor's Degree, Doctorate, High School, and Master's Degree. This helps identify the relationship between education and customer characteristics.

Occupation Segmentation
Customers are segmented into different occupational categories such as Artist, Doctor, Engineer, Entrepreneur, Lawyer, Manager, Nurse, and Salesperson. This provides insight into the composition of the customer base.

Premium Amount Analysis
Premium amounts are analyzed across gender and education-level combinations. This helps identify customer groups that contribute significantly to overall premium revenue.

Customer Communication Preferences
The dashboard analyzes preferred communication methods, including email, email in-person meetings, email mail, and email phone. This can help organizations understand how customers prefer to communicate.

